There are two sequels and spinoffs, but neither one,

00:32:14.420 --> 00:32:16.560
well, let's start with the first one that's interesting,

00:32:16.580 --> 00:32:21.400
is that there was a Game Boy version being worked on of Shadow of the Ninja,

00:32:21.830 --> 00:32:26.920
but the project was reworked and re-released as Ninja Gaiden Shadow,

00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:31.900
which is very interesting because that's not even the same publisher.

00:32:32.180 --> 00:32:34.560
Like, this is now Ninja Gaiden's under Tecmo,

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:39.660
so they took a Shadow of the Ninja game and turned it into a Ninja Gaiden game,

00:32:39.700 --> 00:32:43.240
and if you look at Ninja Gaiden Shadow,

00:32:43.580 --> 00:32:46.820
which I guess keeps, it's kind of like a combination of the two,

00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:50.940
a lot of it is obviously with Ryu,

00:32:51.160 --> 00:32:53.480
but he, it looks like Ninja Gaiden,

00:32:53.660 --> 00:32:56.440
but it plays like Shadow of the Ninja,

00:32:56.440 --> 00:32:58.980
that there is still a lot of, you know,

00:32:59.080 --> 00:33:03.040
hanging from platforms and a lot of similar,

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:08.040
like enemies and mechanics from this NES game brought over to the Game Boy 1,

00:33:08.100 --> 00:33:11.160
so I see it for sure that it was going to be Shadow of the Ninja.

00:33:11.340 --> 00:33:15.720
I just wonder, how do you change, like, hands that far,

00:33:15.880 --> 00:33:19.520
that it becomes a completely different franchise that you don't own?

00:33:19.520 --> 00:33:22.120
It sounds like, from what you're saying,

00:33:22.280 --> 00:33:24.240
it sounds like they made Ninja Gaiden Gaiden.

00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:30.480
Right, right. Like a true Gaiden game that has nothing really to do with the original,

00:33:30.660 --> 00:33:32.000
with the actual franchise,

00:33:32.200 --> 00:33:34.540
and it's like, oh, we'll still put the name on it.

00:33:34.960 --> 00:33:38.620
That might not be how, like, Gaiden games get made,

00:33:38.780 --> 00:33:40.420
but that's how I'm choosing to see it.

00:33:40.420 --> 00:33:44.560
And then in 2024, two years ago,

00:33:44.820 --> 00:33:47.920
we would have said last year, not too long ago,

00:33:48.740 --> 00:33:50.400
Shadow of the Ninja Reborn.

00:33:50.520 --> 00:33:51.820
And next year, right.

00:33:52.940 --> 00:33:58.000
Shadow of the Ninja Reborn was released on basically everything,

00:33:58.300 --> 00:34:01.200
Switch, PS5, Xbox Series X, Steam.

00:34:01.660 --> 00:34:02.800
And this looks,

00:34:03.940 --> 00:34:07.380
they simultaneously made a very good-looking game, in my view,

00:34:07.380 --> 00:34:11.040
like, kind of a metal slug-looking-ish game,

00:34:11.180 --> 00:34:16.220
but also retaining a lot of the aesthetic of this NES game,

00:34:16.280 --> 00:34:17.680
so kudos to them on that.

00:34:17.920 --> 00:34:20.720
But this game looks very flashy and fun,

00:34:20.740 --> 00:34:23.000
from what I'm seeing here.

00:34:23.020 --> 00:34:27.080
It looks like they just took the ideas from this NES game

00:34:27.080 --> 00:34:29.000
and expanded on it times 100.

00:34:29.940 --> 00:34:34.420
Even the enemies behave similarly to the way they behaved in the NES game,

00:34:34.500 --> 00:34:35.400
but everything just, like,

00:34:36.300 --> 00:34:37.440
you know, again, it's just,

00:34:37.560 --> 00:34:40.820
it's more colorful, more polished,

00:34:41.040 --> 00:34:44.380
more, just a beautiful art style here.

00:34:44.720 --> 00:34:48.320
However, the game seems to have a reputation for being very hard, too.

00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:52.680
So I don't know if I would pay the bucks to see this one,

00:34:52.800 --> 00:34:54.740
but visually, just looking at a gameplay thing,

00:34:54.880 --> 00:34:57.860
like, it's very mesmerizing to look at.

00:34:57.960 --> 00:34:58.880
So if anyone's played it,

00:34:59.100 --> 00:35:01.920
would love to hear if it holds up.

00:35:01.920 --> 00:35:04.880
Because it, yeah, it looks like a true, like,

00:35:04.980 --> 00:35:06.900
we're inspired by the original game,

00:35:07.020 --> 00:35:08.440
and we finally went back and made it.

00:35:08.560 --> 00:35:12.500
Like, that's very interesting that Netsumi seems to be doing this

00:35:13.200 --> 00:35:15.520
with their games, going back into the catalog.

00:35:16.100 --> 00:35:18.040
I could be convinced to play this.

00:35:18.220 --> 00:35:22.880
Could I convince you to move on and do the Essential Games list?

00:35:27.160 --> 00:35:32.440
Shadow of the Ninja is coming in as a recommend from me,

00:35:32.640 --> 00:35:36.600
especially if you've been enjoying these other ninja games that we've had.

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:40.700
And this might just be where it falls in the list,

00:35:40.700 --> 00:35:41.900
and it just gets, like, shitty,

00:35:42.020 --> 00:35:45.360
which is kind of upsetting because it's also alphabetical when it comes down to month.

00:35:45.360 --> 00:35:47.860
But at this point, I'm a little tired.

00:35:48.320 --> 00:35:50.900
We've had Little Ninja Brothers.

00:35:51.180 --> 00:35:52.100
We've had Ninja Crusaders.

00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:53.780
Now we have Shadow of the Ninja.

00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:57.740
Technically, I guess you could count Jackie Chan's Action Kung Fu in there as well.

00:35:58.100 --> 00:36:00.660
So it just feels like all a little played out for me,

00:36:00.720 --> 00:36:02.080
and it's not sticking anymore.

00:36:02.280 --> 00:36:05.740
Like, this game doesn't stand out enough to warrant it.

00:36:06.020 --> 00:36:07.860
And that also makes me worried about,

00:36:07.860 --> 00:36:11.120
I remember Joe voting Essential on Ninja Crusaders,

00:36:11.120 --> 00:36:13.080
and I was like, I want to hold off.

00:36:13.080 --> 00:36:15.800
Now I'm worried that I'm not going to be too hype on that game.

00:36:16.660 --> 00:36:18.580
So I guess what I'm saying is that, like,

00:36:18.640 --> 00:36:20.440
there actually is genre fatigue,

00:36:21.260 --> 00:36:24.960
even when you're exposed to it, like, years later.

00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:30.020
Like, I'm somehow as fatigued as probably people were at this time with ninja stuff.

00:36:30.200 --> 00:36:32.400
Of, like, you know, all of a sudden,

00:36:32.560 --> 00:36:35.200
Digger T-Rock Legend of the Lost City is looking pretty good.

00:36:35.300 --> 00:36:36.960
Like, yeah, we don't have enough caveman games.

00:36:39.920 --> 00:36:41.280
So it's a no from me.

00:36:41.600 --> 00:36:45.720
Sean? I'd say of the ninja games that we've played,

00:36:46.680 --> 00:36:48.620
I've had the most fun with this one.

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:54.220
I don't really have real, like, complaints with the game,

00:36:54.380 --> 00:36:56.980
aside from some, like,

00:36:57.680 --> 00:37:01.660
like, not being very clear on if you're doing damage to bosses,

00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:03.920
even though some of them are very,

00:37:04.400 --> 00:37:06.280
it's very obvious that you're doing damage.

00:37:06.280 --> 00:37:08.720
There's a guy that just sort of, like, blows up

00:37:08.720 --> 00:37:10.880
when you hit him a few times.

00:37:12.440 --> 00:37:14.740
But he comes back together at the end.

00:37:15.460 --> 00:37:17.160
Yeah, so I really like this game.

00:37:17.360 --> 00:37:21.180
I also might have some ninja fatigue, though,

00:37:21.880 --> 00:37:25.600
with just how frequently they're coming up recently.

00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:29.120
So I don't know if I can put this on the essential games list right now.

00:37:29.120 --> 00:37:32.920
But, you know, I don't quite remember Ninja Crusaders.

00:37:33.220 --> 00:37:40.560
So maybe once we've sort of done a once-over,

00:37:40.560 --> 00:37:42.560
we can think about it.

00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:44.500
So not essential for now.

00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:46.860
Joe? Yeah, this was pretty fun.

00:37:46.960 --> 00:37:48.080
I thought it was a fun game.

00:37:48.460 --> 00:37:53.880
I think that the word mediocre is kind of, like, a mean word.

00:37:54.020 --> 00:37:58.700
And I feel like mediocre means, like, you know,

00:37:58.780 --> 00:38:00.860
it's not terrible, but, like, it's not great.

00:38:00.860 --> 00:38:02.900
And it's used in, like, a negative way.

00:38:03.060 --> 00:38:06.060
And I want to find, like, the other side of mediocre where it's like...

00:38:06.060 --> 00:38:08.960
Solid. Yeah, it's not amazing, but, like, it's all right.

00:38:09.320 --> 00:38:10.400
You know, like, that's kind of, like,

00:38:10.440 --> 00:38:13.620
I think that mediocre also technically might count there,

00:38:13.700 --> 00:38:14.820
but it just doesn't sound like it.

00:38:14.820 --> 00:38:15.640
But that's what I mean.

00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:18.020
It's fine. You know, I had fun.

00:38:18.020 --> 00:38:19.140
I think you should play this.

00:38:19.220 --> 00:38:20.760
But, like, I'm not...

00:38:21.340 --> 00:38:23.680
I would not feel right voting at essential.

00:38:23.860 --> 00:38:24.980
So I'm going to say no.

00:38:25.520 --> 00:38:29.060
Sean, your comment about the exploding bosses reminded me that

00:38:29.060 --> 00:38:31.160
this was something that I read about

00:38:31.160 --> 00:38:35.720
but could definitely not, like, recreate in my playthrough

00:38:36.240 --> 00:38:39.080
is that there was a theory, I guess, online

00:38:39.080 --> 00:38:43.820
that how close you are to the explosion of the boss,

00:38:43.820 --> 00:38:47.020
like, dictates how much health replenishes.

00:38:47.300 --> 00:38:51.800
But in my experience, your health just replenishes a little bit,

00:38:52.060 --> 00:38:54.100
like, X amount once you defeat the boss

00:38:54.100 --> 00:38:55.440
and it doesn't matter where in the room

00:38:55.440 --> 00:38:57.340
or how close to the boss you were.

00:38:57.840 --> 00:39:01.180
Interesting. And you're talking about the one specific boss

00:39:01.180 --> 00:39:02.820
or you're talking about bosses in general?

00:39:03.060 --> 00:39:05.140
No, no, yeah, that first boss.

00:39:05.340 --> 00:39:09.400
Oh, yeah. I was also confused because sometimes, like,

00:39:09.460 --> 00:39:11.120
he would explode at you

00:39:11.120 --> 00:39:13.360
and sometimes he would explode away from you

00:39:13.360 --> 00:39:15.240
and I wasn't sure if that was just completely random.

00:39:16.020 --> 00:39:18.820
So it seems like there's a lot of, like,

00:39:19.220 --> 00:39:21.940
just weird randomness going on with that boss.

00:39:22.660 --> 00:39:27.240
Yeah. But also, you know, the bosses in general,

00:39:27.500 --> 00:39:29.520
while it is weird about their hitboxes,

00:39:30.120 --> 00:39:33.740
I did like even just the one-on-one human

00:39:33.740 --> 00:39:37.240
or humanoid characters that you fight in this game.

00:39:37.240 --> 00:39:42.060
They had good behaviors and made for interesting boss fights,

00:39:42.100 --> 00:39:45.740
not just, like, hide in a corner or this is too fucking hard.

00:39:46.460 --> 00:39:49.320
Yeah. But we're not going to revisit the game.

00:39:49.560 --> 00:39:50.780
It's much too soon for that.

00:39:50.920 --> 00:39:54.740
We'll wait till our best of 1990 episode,

00:39:54.740 --> 00:39:55.560
which is coming up.

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:58.540
We have Star Tropics next week.

00:39:58.820 --> 00:39:59.660
Pretty big game.

00:39:59.820 --> 00:40:02.740
A lot of people said that they're going to unsubscribe

00:40:02.740 --> 00:40:04.160
if we don't vote at Essential.

00:40:04.380 --> 00:40:05.680
I'm immune to your threats, people.

00:40:05.680 --> 00:40:06.520
You can't.

00:40:06.980 --> 00:40:08.420
That stuff doesn't work on me.

00:40:08.860 --> 00:40:10.600
You see what I've done with Zelda 2.

00:40:10.780 --> 00:40:13.600
Don't make me do that to Star Tropics.

00:40:14.160 --> 00:40:15.360
On a similar note, though,

00:40:16.100 --> 00:40:17.600
and I don't really know what I meant by that,

00:40:17.680 --> 00:40:20.320
so don't read it. It's too late.

00:40:20.860 --> 00:40:21.940
Cannon, ring that bell.

00:40:22.460 --> 00:40:23.760
You heard it here first.

00:40:23.840 --> 00:40:26.100
He only did it as a political statement.

00:40:26.100 --> 00:40:29.580
I, for one, genuinely don't really like Zelda 2.

00:40:29.820 --> 00:40:30.680
It doesn't matter.

00:40:30.800 --> 00:40:33.140
Me and Mike do, so it would be essential if he wasn't so political.

00:40:33.340 --> 00:40:36.940
Well, we'll see. Anyway, after Star Tropics,

00:40:37.060 --> 00:40:38.900
we have a weird thing going on, okay?

00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:40.240
And I want to make the audience aware of it.

00:40:40.400 --> 00:40:45.360
There are two combo games or compilation games.

00:40:45.440 --> 00:40:48.740
One of them is Super Mario Brothers Duck Hunt World Clash Track Meet,

00:40:49.340 --> 00:40:51.940
and one of them is Super Spike V-Ball Nintendo World Cup.

00:40:52.260 --> 00:40:55.220
We've already played these games, obviously.

00:40:55.500 --> 00:41:03.160
All five of these. Yeah, they're being compiled because I'm sure Nintendo wanted to bundle up some new stuff for the holidays,

00:41:03.840 --> 00:41:07.100
and so I just want to prepare people that we will still do these episodes,

00:41:07.180 --> 00:41:10.000
and we might talk a little bit about these games,

00:41:10.140 --> 00:41:13.460
but I also have other topics that I would like to discuss on these episodes.

00:41:13.620 --> 00:41:15.140
So when you see the titles,

00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:19.400
don't automatically assume that I'm just going to paste three episodes together

00:41:19.400 --> 00:41:21.000
and count that as a new episode.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:26.640
We will have some offbeat shenanigans in those episodes.

00:41:27.700 --> 00:41:29.000
We can't do a Mr.

00:41:29.100 --> 00:41:29.940
Dream thing anymore.

00:41:30.060 --> 00:41:31.040
I was just going to say,

00:41:31.180 --> 00:41:33.600
we should take the word track meet and replace it with Mr.

00:41:33.740 --> 00:41:34.540
Dream every time.

00:41:35.020 --> 00:41:38.400
Right. That was a fun episode, too, though.

00:41:38.500 --> 00:41:45.800
People should listen to that one. We'll be right back.
